## Documentation Carve-Out

Everything above this line is the Functional Source License, Version 1.1,
ALv2 Future License, verbatim apart from the Notice. This section grants
additional rights over part of the repository; it takes nothing away.

The documentation **text** in `docs/` and `apps/docs/` — the Markdown files
and the prose in them — is additionally licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International license (CC BY 4.0),
<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>. You may use that text under
either license, at your option, including for a Competing Use. Attribution is
required: name Orcaops Inc. and link back to the source.

The carve-out covers documentation, not machinery. Source code, build
tooling, and site scaffolding that happen to live under those directories
remain under the Terms and Conditions above, which is also why the manifest
in `apps/docs/` declares the FSL rather than CC BY 4.0.

Brand assets are **not** carved out. Everything under
`apps/docs/content/public/` — the favicon, the orca mark, and the wordmark, in
every variant — stays under the Terms and Conditions above and is excluded
from the CC BY 4.0 grant. A permissive grant over those files would license
copying and modification of the marks themselves for a Competing Use, which
`TRADEMARKS.md` exists to refuse; copyright and trademark are separate rights,
and this carve-out withholds both.

## Third-Party Components

Parts of this repository are third-party source under their own licenses,
with their own notices alongside them:

- `packages/diff-render/` vendors MIT-licensed source — see
  `packages/diff-render/LICENSE` and its `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md`.
- `packages/agent-targets/` vendors MIT-licensed source — see
  `packages/agent-targets/LICENSE`.

The published npm package carries a `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md` covering the
dependencies bundled into it.
